# Indexer Rules

## Framework
- Use Ponder for EVM event indexing
- Schema defined in `ponder.schema.ts` using `onchainTable`
- Event handlers in `src/` — one file per contract
- Import ABIs from `@bounce/shared`

## Patterns
- Use the `"setup"` event for initializing singleton records
- Handle chain reorgs automatically (Ponder does this — don't add custom logic)
- Use `context.db` for database operations within event handlers
- Keep event handlers focused — extract complex calculations to `src/helpers/`
- For exchange rate polling, use Ponder's block-based handlers

## Schema
- Table names are singular (e.g., `token`, `trade`, `creator`)
- Use `hex` type for addresses and transaction hashes
- Include `blockNumber` and `timestamp` on all records for ordering
- Define relations between tables for relational queries

## Performance
- Minimize RPC calls in event handlers — use event data when possible
- Set appropriate `pollingInterval` in config to avoid rate limiting
- Use batch inserts when processing multiple records in one event
